    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's much better, thanks. that \"essential act\" framing is exactly the kind of depth they need. one more thing—in these debates, the opposition usually tries to pivot to the human rights or humanitarian aspect to make the enforcement side look cruel or heartless. can you give them a strong rebuttal to that? basically, how can they argue that prioritizing national sovereignty and law is actually the most ethical approach in the long run, even if it seems harsh in the short term?",
